1037
00:39:00,810 --> 00:39:01,810
Right.

1038
00:39:02,450 --> 00:39:03,610
Tsuki, this is seriously delicious.

1039
00:39:03,810 --> 00:39:05,480
(She made them satisfied perfectly.)

1040
00:39:07,450 --> 00:39:08,750
(Time to eat for me)

1041
00:39:08,820 --> 00:39:09,820
I cannot wait.

1042
00:39:10,450 --> 00:39:11,620
There are only two pieces, though.

1043
00:39:13,820 --> 00:39:15,560
(Finishing in one bite)

1044
00:39:17,960 --> 00:39:19,260
(Wow)

1045
00:39:19,460 --> 00:39:21,460
(Rmenping will try too)

1046
00:39:25,170 --> 00:39:27,470
(BamBam is ready for Mukbang.)

1047
00:39:27,470 --> 00:39:29,670
(Manners hand)

1048
00:39:30,410 --> 00:39:32,940
(His mouth is full.)

1049
00:39:32,940 --> 00:39:35,440
(What is Lele doing?)

1050
00:39:35,640 --> 00:39:37,250
(Could it not suit his taste?)

1051
00:39:37,580 --> 00:39:38,580
What do you think, Chenle?

1052
00:39:38,650 --> 00:39:40,550
Chenle, who is also great at cooking.

1053
00:39:40,550 --> 00:39:42,620
(Clean)

1054
00:39:43,390 --> 00:39:45,450
- With his actions. - This is my review.

1055
00:39:46,660 --> 00:39:48,020
Honestly, I was really worried.

1056
00:39:48,020 --> 00:39:51,190
Since he was not saying anything, I wondered if he did not like it.

1057
00:39:51,260 --> 00:39:53,130
- You were too busy eating to talk. - This is my review.

1058
00:39:54,360 --> 00:39:55,660
(Eating,)

1059
00:39:55,660 --> 00:39:57,470
(eating and eating again)

1060
00:39:57,570 --> 00:39:59,140
(Taking another big bite)

1061
00:39:59,170 --> 00:40:00,570
(The Mukbang brakes are broken.)

1062
00:40:00,970 --> 00:40:01,970
This is so delicious.

1063
00:40:03,110 --> 00:40:04,710
(Tsuki is excited.)

1064
00:40:04,710 --> 00:40:05,710
It is really delicious.

1065
00:40:06,340 --> 00:40:08,410
It's a great light snack. It has...

1066
00:40:08,410 --> 00:40:09,450
Just the right amount of kick.

1067
00:40:09,510 --> 00:40:11,010
- It has everything it needs. - I agree.

1068
00:40:11,150 --> 00:40:14,850
And while having a very Korean feel,

1069
00:40:15,250 --> 00:40:16,950
you can also taste a hint of Japan.

1070
00:40:17,050 --> 00:40:18,750
Because of the bonito flakes and mayonnaise,

1071
00:40:19,050 --> 00:40:20,990
it reminds me a bit of Takoyaki at first.

1072
00:40:21,060 --> 00:40:22,160
- That is right. - Selling this in Japan...

1073
00:40:22,160 --> 00:40:23,660
would probably be a huge hit.

1074
00:40:23,730 --> 00:40:24,990
(Spicy Pork and Bean Sprout Tonpeiyaki)

1075
00:40:25,060 --> 00:40:26,530
I am so curious about this one too.

1076
00:40:26,600 --> 00:40:28,400
- So much. - I am really looking forward to it.

1077
00:40:29,030 --> 00:40:32,070
(We can't wait to eat dessert.)

1078
00:40:32,070 --> 00:40:33,700
(Exclaiming)

1079
00:40:33,700 --> 00:40:35,770
(Anyway, they are satisfied with the taste.)

1080
00:40:36,270 --> 00:40:37,270
Thank you for the meal.

1081
00:40:38,870 --> 00:40:40,240
(Being nervous again)

1082
00:40:41,440 --> 00:40:45,750
(Will it suit his taste?)

1083
00:40:45,980 --> 00:40:46,980
What?

1084
00:40:48,150 --> 00:40:51,350
Combining soybean powder with cheese makes this taste so good.

1085
00:40:51,450 --> 00:40:52,760
It is nutty yet savory.

1086
00:40:53,160 --> 00:40:56,360
The soybean powder rounds out the aftertaste nicely.

1087
00:40:56,690 --> 00:40:57,690
I like it.

1088
00:40:57,960 --> 00:41:00,030
The thick sauce tastes just like the spicy fried rice cake skewers,

1089
00:41:00,100 --> 00:41:01,260
- Right. - so it feels nostalgic.

1090
00:41:01,260 --> 00:41:02,830
Right, rather than tteokbokki,

1091
00:41:02,900 --> 00:41:04,230
it is closer to spicy fried rice cake skewers.

1092
00:41:05,070 --> 00:41:06,540
People usually think Dango is sweet,

1093
00:41:06,600 --> 00:41:08,670
but Dango itself is not really sweet.

1094
00:41:09,470 --> 00:41:12,110
It is just like plain rice cakes. That is why the sauce is actually...

1095
00:41:12,170 --> 00:41:14,840
a little bit heavily seasoned, which makes it go together so well.

1096
00:41:14,940 --> 00:41:16,210
- It goes so well. - It goes so well.

1097
00:41:16,280 --> 00:41:17,910
I cannot wait. I am so excited.

1098
00:41:18,850 --> 00:41:21,680
(Dream Chefs Tasting Session)

1099
00:41:21,750 --> 00:41:23,520
You love tteokbokki so much, Carmen.

1100
00:41:23,520 --> 00:41:24,590
(Wow)

1101
00:41:26,260 --> 00:41:27,360
(Nodding in Perfect Sync)

1102
00:41:27,660 --> 00:41:32,700
(Rmenping is also taking a bite of Dango Skewer.)

1103
00:41:32,800 --> 00:41:35,200
- I want to take this to go. To go. - Just like this.

1104
00:41:35,660 --> 00:41:36,730
No, you can just finish this...

1105
00:41:36,970 --> 00:41:39,000
- and ask her to make more. - Yes.

1106
00:41:40,270 --> 00:41:41,270
Is it just me?

1107
00:41:41,370 --> 00:41:43,970
Why do I want to put bacon in instead of fish cake?

1108
00:41:44,270 --> 00:41:46,310
- Because it tastes like bacon? - That would go well together too.

1109
00:41:46,310 --> 00:41:47,880
- That sounds good. - I don't know...

1110
00:41:47,880 --> 00:41:49,280
it's because it's bite-sized,

1111
00:41:49,280 --> 00:41:51,380
but having something like a quail egg right in the middle...

1112
00:41:51,380 --> 00:41:53,050
- A quail egg. - Like that.

1113
00:41:53,280 --> 00:41:55,350
- I love that. - If you do it that way,

1114
00:41:55,450 --> 00:41:56,450
- that would be really nice. - The best.

1115
00:41:56,750 --> 00:41:58,890
Tsuki, you might need to wipe your mouth...

1116
00:41:58,890 --> 00:42:00,760
with a tissue first, though.

1117
00:42:02,690 --> 00:42:05,460
(Laughing)

1118
00:42:05,460 --> 00:42:07,860
- Please share your recipe. - Right.

1119
00:42:08,060 --> 00:42:09,870
I really hope everyone would follow this recipe.

1120
00:42:10,070 --> 00:42:13,500
(Spicy Pork and Bean Sprout Tonpeiyaki Recipe Details)

1121
00:42:13,570 --> 00:42:17,010
(Mitarashi Dango Skewer Recipe Details)

1122
00:42:17,070 --> 00:42:19,380
Now, Tsuki's dishes,

1123
00:42:19,380 --> 00:42:20,410
which captured our taste buds today,

1124
00:42:20,480 --> 00:42:24,350
